{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# Is there a 3-pt configuration with an LR selection rule?\n\n**Question (Paul).** The note's configuration has no LR selection rule. Is there another pair of globally rotated BPS states (bridge blocks) such that ⟨B|Ψ⟩ = 0 unless Ψ is LR symmetric?\n\n**Configurations.** O₁ (2L sites, A F A F …) has its first block (ℓ consecutive sites, starting on an A site or on an F site) contracted with O₂ and the rest with O₃. Each block is a globally rotated vacuum: A sites carry a vector a, F sites f, with a·f = 0 (bilinear). Under global GL(4) (A by g, F by g^{−T}) and rescalings, a pair of blocks (a₁,f₁), (a₂,f₂) is classified by which cross pairings a₁·f₂, a₂·f₁ vanish and by linear dependences; representatives (block 1 = (e₁, e₄)):\n\n| orbit | block 2 (a₂, f₂) | a₁·f₂ | a₂·f₁ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| generic (= note, W₋₁) | (e₁−e₄, e₄+e₁) | ≠ 0 | ≠ 0 |\n| a₂·f₁ = 0 | (e₂, e₁+e₃) | ≠ 0 | 0 |\n| a₁·f₂ = 0 | (e₄+e₂, e₃) | 0 | ≠ 0 |\n| both 0 | (e₂, e₃) | 0 | 0 |\n| a₂ = a₁ | (e₁, e₃) | 0 | 0 |\n| f₂ = f₁ | (e₂, e₄) | 0 | 0 |\n\nWithin an orbit the polarisations differ by a global rotation g, which only moves within an su(4) multiplet. So for each (orbit, ℓ, start) the overlap of the whole multiplet of Ψ is probed by ⟨B|g|Ψ_HW⟩ over random g: the state **couples** iff this is nonzero for some g.\n\n**Test.** For every configuration and L = 2, 3, 4 pairs (saved states, `data/abjm-hw-states.wxf`): count coupling non-LR states and coupling LR states (excluding the BPS vacuum multiplet). A selection rule = no non-LR state couples, some non-BPS LR state does.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "nn = 4; dataFile = \"c:\\\\Users\\\\pryan\\\\git-projects\\\\abjm-c123\\\\Paul\\\\Mathematica\\\\su4-alternating\\\\data\\\\abjm-hw-states.wxf\";\nstates = Import[dataFile, \"WXF\"];\nev[i_] := UnitVector[nn, i];\norbits = {{\"generic (note)\", {ev[1] - ev[4], ev[4] + ev[1]}}, {\"a2.f1 = 0\", {ev[2], ev[1] + ev[3]}}, {\"a1.f2 = 0\", {ev[4] + ev[2], ev[3]}},\n   {\"both 0\", {ev[2], ev[3]}}, {\"a2 = a1\", {ev[1], ev[3]}}, {\"f2 = f1\", {ev[2], ev[4]}}};\nblock1 = {ev[1], ev[4]};\n(* bra for 2L = LL sites: sites start..start+l-1 (cyclic) in block 1, rest in block 2; odd sites A (vector a), even sites F (vector f); global g *)\nbraConf[LL_, start_, l_, b2_, g_] := Module[{inB1 = Mod[start - 1 + Range[0, l - 1], LL] + 1, gi = Transpose[Inverse[g]]},\n   Flatten[Outer[Times, Sequence @@ Table[With[{b = If[MemberQ[inB1, s], block1, b2]}, If[OddQ[s], g . b[[1]], gi . b[[2]]]], {s, LL}]]]];\nSeedRandom[2026]; gs = Table[RandomComplex[{-1 - I, 1 + I}, {nn, nn}], 6];\nisBPS[st_, L_] := st[\"dyn\"] == {L, 0, L};\nscanConf[L_, orb_, l_, start_] := Module[{LL = 2 L, sts = states[\"L\" <> ToString[L]], bras, C, cpl},\n   bras = Table[braConf[LL, start, l, orb[[2]], g], {g, gs}];\n   C = Table[Max[Abs[(# . Normal[st[\"psi\"]]) & /@ bras]], {st, sts}];\n   cpl = Thread[C > 10^-9];\n   {L, orb[[1]], l, If[start == 1, \"A\", \"F\"],\n    Count[Transpose[{sts, cpl}], {s_, True} /; s[\"LR\"] >= 10^-8],\n    Count[Transpose[{sts, cpl}], {s_, True} /; s[\"LR\"] < 10^-8 && !isBPS[s, L]],\n    Count[sts, s_ /; s[\"LR\"] >= 10^-8], Count[sts, s_ /; s[\"LR\"] < 10^-8 && !isBPS[s, L]]}];\nscan[L_] := Flatten[Table[scanConf[L, orb, l, start], {orb, orbits}, {l, 1, 2 L - 1}, {start, {1, 2}}], 2];\nscan2 = scan[2];\nGrid[Prepend[scan2, {\"L\", \"orbit\", \"ℓ\", \"start\", \"# non-LR coupling\", \"# non-BPS LR coupling\", \"# non-LR total\", \"# non-BPS LR total\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"825950\" data-output-id=\"64\" data-out-n=\"642\" data-sub-idx=\"12\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"1\" data-sub-start=\"21\" data-sub-end=\"21\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[642]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"15\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:44.44em;vertical-align:-21.95em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:22.49em;\"><span style=\"top:-24.45em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:24.45em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:44.4em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-21.95em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:22.45em;\"><span style=\"top:-24.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">L</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-23.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-22.21em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-21.01em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">2</span></span></span><span style=\"to