  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Summary (2026-10-12)\n\nAll two-block BPS configurations (6 GL(4) orbits of the polarisation pair × every bridge length ℓ × bridge starting on A or F; 180 configurations at L = 2, 3, 4 pairs), whole multiplets probed by random global rotations:\n\n- **No configuration has an LR selection rule that persists.** \"Only LR states couple\" happens only at L = 2 (orbit both-zero, ℓ = 2, one LR state). At L = 3 and L = 4 every configuration that couples to any non-BPS LR state also couples to non-LR states.\n- The **generic orbit is the note's configuration** (any two BPS blocks with a₁·f₂ ≠ 0 ≠ a₂·f₁ are GL(4)-equivalent to (e₁,e₄) | (e₁−e₄, e₄+e₁)), so changing polarisations within it cannot create a rule.\n- The opposite happens often: \"only non-LR states couple\" in 8, 14, 24 configurations at L = 2, 3, 4 (e.g. generic ℓ = 1, 2L−1 at L = 2, 4; half-degenerate orbits at specific ℓ), but the pattern is not uniform in L (generic ℓ = 1 is \"both\" at L = 3).\n- Caveat: probing multiplets by random rotations makes p ≠ r and q ≠ 0 states reachable, which the note's HW-projected table did not see; \"non-LR\" includes those.\n\nInterpretation: in 2603 the rule comes from ⟨W|(t₊ − t₋) = 0 for the BPS bra plus the bridge operator being built from transfer matrices. For ABJM, single globally rotated BPS blocks never give such a bra here; an LR rule would need a bra annihilated by t̄₁(u) − t̄₃(u+h), which no two-block BPS bra is (at L = 3, 4).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Parity-type selection rules for the same length-independent configurations\n\nSame two-block BPS bras B_{L,ℓ} (block 1 = (e₁, e₄), block 2 from one of the 6 orbits, the **same vectors for every L**), now testing the other symmetries of `abjm-other-symmetries.wb`: P (τ̄₁(u) = τ̄₁(2h−u)) and LP (τ̄₁(u) = τ̄₃(3h−u)). A configuration has a P (LP) selection rule if no non-P (non-LP) state couples while some non-BPS P (LP) state does. Hits are cross-checked by the operator identity B·X(u)r = 0 on random kets at L = 2, 3, 4.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "tauAll = Import[FileNameJoin[{DirectoryName[dataFile], \"abjm-tau.wxf\"}], \"WXF\"];\nrelFit2[cA_, cB_, sign_] := Module[{n = Length[cA] - 1, c, x, d},\n   c = If[sign == -1, -(cA[[n]] + cB[[n]])/(n cB[[n + 1]]), (cA[[n]] - cB[[n]])/(n cB[[n + 1]])];\n   d = CoefficientList[Expand[cA . x^Range[0, n] - cB . (If[sign == -1, c - x, x + c])^Range[0, n]], x]; Max[Abs[d]]/Max[Abs[cA]] < 10^-8];\nsymFlags[L_] := Table[<|\"LR\" -> relFit2[tc[[1]], tc[[3]], 1], \"P\" -> relFit2[tc[[1]], tc[[1]], -1], \"LP\" -> relFit2[tc[[1]], tc[[3]], -1]|>, {tc, tauAll[\"L\" <> ToString[L]]}];\nflags = Association[Table[L -> symFlags[L], {L, {2, 3, 4}}]];\nscanSym[L_, orb_, l_, start_, kind_] := Module[{LL = 2 L, sts = states[\"L\" <> ToString[L]], bras, cpl, fl = flags[L]},\n   bras = Table[braConf[LL, start, l, orb[[2]], g], {g, gs}];\n   cpl = Table[Max[Abs[(# . Normal[st[\"psi\"]]) & /@ bras]] > 10^-9, {st, sts}];\n   {L, orb[[1]], l, If[start == 1, \"A\", \"F\"], kind,\n    Count[Range[Length[sts]], i_ /; cpl[[i]] && !fl[[i, kind]]],\n    Count[Range[Length[sts]], i_ /; cpl[[i]] && fl[[i, kind]] && !isBPS[sts[[i]], L]]}];\nsymScan = Flatten[Table[scanSym[L, orb, l, start, kind], {kind, {\"P\", \"LP\"}}, {L, {2, 3, 4}}, {orb, orbits}, {l, 1, 2 L - 1}, {start, {1, 2}}], 4];\nhits = Select[symScan, #[[6]] == 0 && #[[7]] > 0 &];\n(* configurations (orbit, l relative to L, start) that are hits at all three lengths: compare with l and with 2L - l *)\nhitKeys[kind_] := GroupBy[Select[hits, #[[5]] == kind &], {#[[2]], #[[4]]} &, Map[{#[[1]], #[[3]]} &]];\nGrid[{{\"# configurations scanned\", Length[symScan]}, {\"# hits P\", Count[hits, h_ /; h[[5]] == \"P\"]}, {\"# hits LP\", Count[hits, h_ /; h[[5]] == \"LP\"]},\n  {\"P hits {orbit, start} → {L, ℓ}\", hitKeys[\"P\"]}, {\"LP hits {orbit, start} → {L, ℓ}\", hitKeys[\"LP\"]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
