  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Summary: length-independent configurations with a selection rule (2026-10-12)\n\nTwo-block BPS bras B_{L,ℓ} = (block 1 on ℓ sites) ⊗ (block 2 on 2L−ℓ sites), block 1 = (a₁,f₁) = (e₁,e₄), block 2 from one of the 6 orbits, **same polarisations for all L**. Operator-level check: ⟨B|X(u)|r⟩ = 0 for all cyclic kets r (equivalently, Σ_k ⟨B|S^k is annihilated), 10⁻¹⁶ at L = 3, 4 (at L = 2 every cyclic state is P-symmetric, so the statement is empty there).\n\n**P (parity, τ̄₁(u) = τ̄₁(2h−u) ⇔ Q₁(u) ∝ Q₁₂₃(2h−u)) selection rules:**\n- the note's configuration (generic orbit, block 2 = (e₁−e₄, e₄+e₁)) with **ℓ = 1** (or 2L−1), bridge starting on A or F;\n- half-degenerate orbits at ℓ = 1: block 2 with a₂·f₁ = 0 (bridge on A) or a₁·f₂ = 0 (bridge on F);\n- both cross pairings zero (block 2 = (e₂, e₃)), **ℓ = 2** (or 2L−2), either start.\n\nFor these, C vanishes for every state that is not P-symmetric, at every length checked; the control (note's configuration at ℓ = 2) fails (10⁻²·⁴).\n\n**LR and LP:** no configuration in this class has a uniform-in-L rule.",
